{
  "title": "CanvasSizingMetrics",
  "description": "One complete description of how the canvas is sized, in the three axes the engine keeps apart. `cssWidth`/`cssHeight` are the element's display box in CSS pixels, or `null` to leave the box exactly as it is - the form a policy uses when the surrounding page owns the canvas geometry. They are ignored for a surface with no document element. `logicalWidth`/`logicalHeight` are the coordinate system the application draws in: node positions, Application.width/Application.height and pointer coordinates are all expressed in it. `renderWidth`/`renderHeight` are the requested render resolution, also in CSS pixels. The backing store becomes `render x pixelRatio`, so a policy states how many pixels it wants without ever applying the device pixel ratio itself.",
